OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20250808
LR  - 20250808
IS  - 1879-8365 (Electronic)
IS  - 0926-9630 (Linking)
VI  - 329
DP  - 2025 Aug 7
TI  - Large Language Model Empowered Privacy-Protected Framework for PHI Annotation in 
      Clinical Notes.
PG  - 876-880
LID - 10.3233/SHTI250965 [doi]
AB  - De-identifying private information in medical records is crucial to prevent 
      confidentiality breaches. Rule-based and learning-based methods struggle with 
      generalizability and require large annotated datasets, while LLMs offer better 
      language comprehension but face privacy risks and high computational costs. We 
      propose LPPA, an LLM-empowered Privacy-protected PHI Annotation framework, which 
      uses few-shot learning with pre-trained LLMs to generate synthetic clinical 
      notes, reducing the need for extensive datasets. By fine-tuning LLMs locally with 
      synthetic notes, LPPA ensures strong privacy protection and high PHI annotation 
      accuracy. Experiments confirm its effectiveness, efficiency, and scalability.
