VI  - 329
DP  - 2025 Aug 7
TI  - Development of a Digital Case-Based Knowledge Base to Support Rapid Learning in 
      Precision Oncology.
PG  - 263-267
LID - 10.3233/SHTI250842 [doi]
AB  - Precision oncology hinges on the exchange of continuously evolving diagnostic and 
      treatment knowledges, with individual patients providing valuable knowledge to 
      supplement frequent scenarios where there are insufficient clinical trials 
      evidence to inform care. We propose a novel architecture of a collaborative 
      web-based community platform to support a learning health concept, organising 
      physician-directed knowledge analysis to support rapid learning. This platform 
      promotes knowledge sharing through systematic organisation and structuring of 
      case studies. A database was structured to systematically curate case reports 
      into the format of clinical scenarios, questions and solutions with the concepts 
      extracted by natural language processing (NLP) and indexed to enable 
      searchability. Clinicians can access this structured knowledge through a 
      web-based question-answering interface to gain rapid insights from relevant cases 
      and discussions. This enables continuous integration of the latest insights and 
      case critiques, providing asynchronous knowledge sharing between clinicians. This 
      platform facilitates rapid learning to address the challenge of evolving oncology 
      knowledge and enhance decision-making, fostering collaboration within the 
      oncology community.
