OAB - We used acoustic analysis and Natural Language Processing (NLP) to evaluate 
      speech data from 66 individuals with psychosis, over time. The study identified 
      specific language features that correlate with different psychosis symptoms as 
      they changed over time. These insights could lead to innovative, non-invasive 
      tools for monitoring schizophrenia and related disorders, enhancing personalized 
      treatment approaches in psychiatry.
