PMID- 40039172
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20250511
LR  - 20250511
IS  - 2694-0604 (Electronic)
IS  - 2375-7477 (Linking)
VI  - 2024
DP  - 2024 Jul
TI  - Fast Rule-based NER in SpaCy for Chest Radiography Reports with CheXpert's 14 
      Categories().
PG  - 1-4
LID - 10.1109/EMBC53108.2024.10782341 [doi]
AB  - Chest X-ray imaging is widely used in medical examinations, with 2 billion 
      performed globally annually. Interpreting X-ray images is time-consuming, 
      prompting the development of AI-assisted systems. Generating a large set of 
      high-quality labeled images is crucial for training accurate and unbiased deep 
      learning models. However, creating high-quality labeled images is challenging. 
      Utilizing Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Named Entity Recognition (NER), 
      we can expedite this process by extracting diagnostic information from text 
      reports. In this study, we developed a rule-based NER tool in SpaCy that can 
      recognize the words and expressions defined in CheXpert's 14 categories. We 
      tested our software using the U.S. National Library of Medicine Open-i dataset. 
      It achieved equivalent accuracy in labeling medical terms with one-sixth the 
      computational time compared to the CheXpert Labeler. This approach holds promise 
      to improve the efficiency of labeling of X-ray images for training AI models to 
      be more accurate in detecting abnormality.Clinical Relevance- This study applied 
      SpaCy NER to label chest X-ray reports with the 14 CheXpert's diagnostic 
      categories with high accuracy. This could reduce human labeling time and error in 
      generating high-quality training datasets for training automated medical imaging 
      analysis software to reduce the burden on doctors.
