VI  - 315
DP  - 2024 Jul 24
TI  - Unveiling Fall Risk Factors: Nurse-Driven Corpus Development for Natural Language 
      Processing.
PG  - 373-378
LID - 10.3233/SHTI240172 [doi]
AB  - Hospital-acquired falls are a continuing clinical concern. The emergence of 
      advanced analytical methods, including NLP, has created opportunities to leverage 
      nurse-generated data, such as clinical notes, to better address the problem of 
      falls. In this nurse-driven study, we employed an iterative process for expert 
      manual annotation of RNs clinical notes to enable the training and testing of an 
      NLP pipeline to extract factors related to falls. The resulting annotated data 
      corpus had moderately high interrater reliability (F-score=0.74) and captured a 
      breadth of clinical concepts for extraction with potential utility beyond patient 
      falls. Further research is needed to determine which annotation tasks most 
      benefit from nursing expert annotators, to optimize efficiency when tapping into 
      the invaluable resource represented by the nursing workforce.
