TI  - The Emerging Role of Artificial Intelligence in Valvular Heart Disease.
PG  - 391-405
LID - S1551-7136(23)00030-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.hfc.2023.03.001 [doi]
AB  - Valvular heart disease (VHD) is a morbid condition in which timely identification 
      and evidence-based treatments can lead to improved outcomes. Artificial 
      intelligence broadly refers to the ability for computers to perform tasks and 
      problem solve like the human mind. Studies applying AI to VHD have used a variety 
      of structured (eg, sociodemographic, clinical) and unstructured (eg, 
      electrocardiogram, phonocardiogram, and echocardiograms) and machine learning 
      modeling approaches. Additional researches in diverse populations, including 
      prospective clinical trials, are needed to evaluate the effectiveness and value 
      of AI-enabled medical technologies in clinical care for patients with VHD.
