TI  - Professionalism and clinical short answer question marking with machine learning.
PG  - 1268-1271
LID - 10.1111/imj.15839 [doi]
AB  - Machine learning may assist in medical student evaluation. This study involved 
      scoring short answer questions administered at three centres. Bidirectional 
      encoder representations from transformers were particularly effective for 
      professionalism question scoring (accuracy ranging from 41.6% to 92.5%). In the 
      scoring of 3-mark professionalism questions, as compared with clinical questions, 
      machine learning had a lower classification accuracy (P < 0.05). The role of 
      machine learning in medical professionalism evaluation warrants further 
      investigation.
