DP  - 2021 Nov 18
TI  - Extraction of Temporal Structures for Clinical Events in Unlabeled Free-Text 
      Electronic Health Records in Russian.
PG  - 55-56
LID - 10.3233/SHTI210811 [doi]
AB  - The important information about a patient is often stored in a free-form text to 
      describe the events in the patient's medical history. In this work, we propose 
      and evaluate a hybrid approach based on rules and syntactical analysis to 
      normalise temporal expressions and assess uncertainty depending on the remoteness 
      of the event. A dataset of 500 sentences was manually labelled to measure the 
      accuracy. On this dataset, the accuracy of extracting temporal expressions is 
      95,5%, and the accuracy of normalization is 94%. The event extraction accuracy is 
      74.80%. The essential advantage of this work is the implementation of the 
      considered approach for the non-English language where NLP tools are limited.
