TI  - Learning Portuguese Clinical Word Embeddings: A Multi-Specialty and 
      Multi-Institutional Corpus of Clinical Narratives Supporting a Downstream 
      Biomedical Task.
PG  - 123-127
LID - 10.3233/SHTI190196 [doi]
AB  - In this paper, we trained a set of Portuguese clinical word embedding models of 
      different granularities from multi-specialty and multi-institutional clinical 
      narrative datasets. Then, we assessed their impact on a downstream biomedical NLP 
      task of Urinary Tract Infection disease identification. Additionally, we 
      intrinsically evaluated our main model using an adapted version of Bio-SimLex for 
      the Portuguese language. Our empirical results showed that the larger, 
      coarse-grained model achieved a slightly better outcome when compared with the 
      small, fine-grained model in the proposed task. Moreover, we obtained 
      satisfactory results with Bio-SimLex intrinsic evaluation.
