TI  - A Software Application for Mining and Presenting Relevant Cancer Clinical Trials 
      per Cancer Mutation.
PG  - 1176935117711940
LID - 10.1177/1176935117711940 [doi]
LID - 1176935117711940
AB  - ClinicalTrials.org is a popular portal which physicians use to find clinical 
      trials for their patients. However, the current setup of ClinicalTrials.org makes 
      it difficult for oncologists to locate clinical trials for patients based on 
      mutational status. We present CTMine, a system that mines ClinicalTrials.org for 
      clinical trials per cancer mutation and displays the trials in a user-friendly 
      Web application. The system currently lists clinical trials for 6 common genes 
      (ALK, BRAF, ERBB2, EGFR, KIT, and KRAS). The current machine learning model used 
      to identify relevant clinical trials focusing on the above gene mutations had an 
      average 88% precision/recall. As part of this analysis, we compared human versus 
      machine and found that oncologists were unable to reach a consensus on whether a 
      clinical trial mined by CTMine was "relevant" per gene mutation, a finding that 
      highlights an important topic which deems future exploration.
