VI  - 207
DP  - 2014
TI  - Unsupervised information extraction from italian clinical records.
PG  - 340-9
AB  - This paper discusses the application of an unsupervised text mining technique for 
      the extraction of information from clinical records in Italian. The approach 
      includes two steps. First of all, a metathesaurus is exploited together with 
      natural language processing tools to extract the domain entities. Then, 
      clustering is applied to explore relations between entity pairs. The results of a 
      preliminary experiment, performed on the text extracted from 57 medical records 
      containing more than 20,000 potential relations, show how the clustering should 
      be based on the cosine similarity distance rather than the City Block or Hamming 
      ones.
