IS  - 1879-8365 (Electronic)
IS  - 0926-9630 (Linking)
VI  - 192
DP  - 2013
TI  - A rule-based method for continuity of care identification in discharge summaries.
PG  - 1221
AB  - Discharge summaries are an important clinical narrative as they include the 
      continuity of care information. Identification of data contained in their text is 
      a difficult task due to its freeform text and lack of consensus on essential 
      content. This research proposes a rule-based method to verify the presence of 
      information about continuity of care in Portuguese texts, applying Natural 
      Language Processing (NLP) techniques, and based on an annotated medical corpus. 
      After the experiments, 4 rules were defined and applied in the text of 200 
      summaries to identify if they have or not the continuity of care information. 
      This process had resulted in Precision value of 84%, Recall value of 70%, 
      Specificity value of 97% and F-Measure value of 76% related to algorithm 
      evaluation.
