IS  - 1559-4076 (Linking)
VI  - 2009
DP  - 2009 Nov 14
TI  - A clinical use case to evaluate the i2b2 Hive: predicting asthma exacerbations.
PG  - 442-6
AB  - To evaluate the i2b2 Hive as a tool to query, visualize, and extract clinical 
      data, we selected a use case from the i2b2 airways diseases driving biology 
      project: asthma exacerbations prediction. We analyzed the cohort selection and 
      the extraction of the clinical data used by this asthma exacerbations prediction 
      study. The structured data included the asthma diagnosis, birthdate, age, race, 
      sex, height, weight, and BMI. The smoking status is typically only mentioned in 
      clinical notes, and we evaluated the Natural Language Processing (NLP) 
      application embedded in the i2b2 NLP cell to extract the smoking status from 
      history and physical exam reports.Querying structured data was possible with the 
      i2b2 workbench for about half the clinical data elements. The remaining had to be 
      queried using a commercial database management system client. The automated 
      extraction of the smoking status reached a mean precision of 0.79 and a mean 
      specificity of 0.90.
