VI  - 2008
DP  - 2008 Nov 6
TI  - Identification and extraction of family history information from clinical 
      reports.
PG  - 247-51
AB  - Many clinical reports contain family history, which is valuable information for 
      clinical decision support and research. We developed a simple natural language 
      processing algorithm to identify and extract family histories. The algorithm was 
      tested on a set of discharge summaries and outpatient clinic notes. The precision 
      and recall of extracting all diagnoses were 85.12% and 86.93%, respectively. The 
      precision and recall of differentiating family history from patient history 
      diagnoses were 96.30% and 92.86%, respectively. Both the precision and recall of 
      exact family member assignment were 92.31%.
