DP  - 2008 Nov 6
TI  - Using natural language processing for identification of pneumonia cases from 
      clinical records of patients with serologically proven influenza.
PG  - 1165
AB  - The purpose of this study was to determine whether influenza vaccination protects 
      against pneumonia in patients who develop influenza. By parsing a data set of 
      records of 1455 patients with serologically proven influenza using SNOMED CT we 
      found that of the vaccinated patients 19.3% developed pneumonia and of the 
      unvaccinated 20.7%. These data suggest that influenza vaccine does not prevent 
      pneumonias in patients who develop influenza despite immunization with influenza 
      vaccine.
